## 5. Engine Orchestration Model

The doc says *"Each engine is a pure module"* and *"The server remains the sole authority"* but never describes **how the engines interact or what calls them**. This is critical.

### Proposed Orchestration Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    CLIENT["Client (React + Zustand)"] -->|"Sends Intent"| SERVER["Server (tRPC)"]
    SERVER -->|"Dispatches to"| DISPATCHER["Engine Dispatcher"]
    
    DISPATCHER --> COMBAT["Combat Engine"]
    DISPATCHER --> INTIMACY["Intimacy Engine"]
    DISPATCHER --> DIALOGUE["Dialogue Engine"]
    DISPATCHER --> MOVEMENT["Movement Engine"]
    DISPATCHER --> ECONOMY["Economy Engine"]
    DISPATCHER --> QUEST["Quest Engine"]
    
    COMBAT -->|"on defeat"| REPUTATION["Reputation Engine"]
    COMBAT -->|"on purification"| PURIFICATION["Purification Engine"]
    INTIMACY -->|"on scene end"| RELATIONSHIP["Relationship Engine"]
    INTIMACY -->|"on conception"| PREGNANCY["Pregnancy Engine"]
    MOVEMENT -->|"on encounter"| COMBAT
    
    CALENDAR["Calendar Engine"] -->|"day-end tick"| REPUTATION
    CALENDAR -->|"day-end tick"| PREGNANCY
    CALENDAR -->|"day-end tick"| MANOR["Manor Engine"]
    CALENDAR -->|"day-end tick"| NPC_POP["NPC Population Engine"]
    CALENDAR -->|"phase advance"| STATUS["Status Effect Engine"]
    
    SAVE["Save/Load Engine"] -.->|"serializes"| GAME_STATE["GameState"]
    GAME_STATE -.->|"read by all"| DISPATCHER
```

### Missing from the doc:

1. **No `GameState` root interface** — What is the shape of the total game state that all engines read/write?
2. **No intent catalog** — What intents can the client send? (MOVE, TALK, FIGHT, USE_ITEM, etc.)
3. **No engine execution order** — When multiple engines need to run in sequence (e.g., movement → encounter → combat), what's the pipeline?
4. **No event system** — How does one engine signal another? (combat end → reputation update → quest objective check)
5. **No day-end tick orchestration** — The doc mentions multiple things happening at day-end (reputation decay, births, population refresh, crafting jobs, construction timers) but doesn't define the execution order

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Recommendation:** Add a **§5.0 Engine Orchestration** section that defines:
> - The `GameState` root interface
> - The intent → engine routing table
> - The day-end tick sequence
> - The event bus or callback system for inter-engine communication

